@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ Nav                          — top bar, always visible; responsive (mobile/des
     RecitationFollow           — "use client" null leaf (ADR 0028): the ONLY reader piece that subscribes to RecitationContext's per-word state — isolated here so ReaderPager never re-renders on a recited-word tick (that caused per-word flicker + repeated font re-fetch). Watches recitedPage while status==="playing"; when the recited page leaves the visible window it calls the pager's followTo, DEFERRED via queueMicrotask so it runs after commitTo's flushSync unwinds (an inline commit would be guarded-out mid-flush and never retry). Effect: playback keeps the recited page on screen — swiping away snaps back to it
     QuranSafhaViewToggle      — client pill (lg+ only): single/double icon buttons, reads/writes QuranSafhaViewContext. Rendered from SettingsSidebar, not the reader entry
     QuranSpread              — client (rendered by Panel): houses the two-page layout; receives onNavigate from the pager and wires it into its NavigationArrow pair — a plain arrow click calls onNavigate (pager-driven, no route change), while modified/middle clicks fall through to the href. Owns the shared NavigationArrow pair (single-step or pair-step hrefs, `relative z-20` so it always stacks above QuranSafha's absolutely-positioned decoration layers), renders two QuranSafha instances (right=odd/leftPage=even) with gap-0 between them on a static `.fq-spread` row. The single-vs-double DISPLAY is CSS-driven, not JS: it marks the non-current card `.fq-safha-partner`, and globals.css (keyed on `html[data-safha-view="double"] .fq-spread` at lg) reveals the partner + applies the width cap + drops the compensate margin — correct at first paint pre-hydration (ADR 0013 Addendum 4). `useIsLgUp`+view survive ONLY to pick the arrow href (pair-step vs single-step). No longer publishes spread geometry — the `useSpreadMetrics` hook and `--fq-spread-width`/`--fq-spread-center` CSS custom properties were retired when the desktop recitation bar moved to a viewport-anchored vertical rail (≥1367px) that needs no spread position data
-      QuranSafha               — client shell: handles word selection, mark state, scroll; accepts grantId (undefined = own mushaf); `lines`/`pageMetadata` are NULLABLE — the card renders its loading state from the page number alone rather than through a separate skeleton component (a duplicate drifts from the layout it imitates; ADR 0034), with the shimmer overlay triggered by `!fontReady || !hasContent` so the content wait and the font wait read as one continuous state instead of two blanks. The header is the card's ONLY content-dependent dimension (the text area is `flex: 1 1 0%`; the card width is floored by the worst-case line-width formula), so juz and the surah glyph fall back to a non-breaking space — leave them empty and the header grows when the JSON lands, shrinking the text area and shifting every skeleton line under it; reads QuranMushafContext — sets the container fontFamily from the active edition (`edition.fontFamily(page)`) and adds the `.fq-tajweed` marker class when the edition uses colour glyphs (selects the themed @font-palette-values rule in globals.css, ADR 0023); no decorative frame — plain bg-card + shadow, square corners; 4 offset "stacked pages" layers in the markup, but only 2 visible below 1367px — the deeper pair carries a bare `hidden` (not `hidden md:block`) and is revealed only by the dark ≥1367px block in globals.css, so tablet and mobile keep the 2-sheet look while desktop dark reads as a thicker block (md+, `bg-card dark:bg-muted` inline classNames — white in light/gold at every width, and in dark theme too outside the reader; a `!important` CSS override in globals.css recolors them to `var(--mushaf-paper)`/`var(--mushaf-edge)` for dark theme specifically at ≥768px in the reader, matching the actual page's paper tone instead of a generic card fill — see dark-theme-mushaf-unification.md Phase 2 — + thin border edge for real contrast, small offset, pointer-events-none so they never intercept clicks); stackPeekSide prop ("left"/"right", default "left") controls which side the stack peeks toward and doubles as a left-page/right-page indicator even in single-page view (always static per pair position, not spread-state-dependent); compensateStackGap prop (default false) tags the card `.fq-compensate-l`/`.fq-compensate-r`; globals.css then reserves a physical 9px margin on the SAME side as stackPeekSide (for the stack's ~9px protrusion) at md+ and removes it only when the spread actually shows both pages — so single-page display keeps both nav arrows equidistant. QuranSpread passes it for both cards; standalone QuranPage leaves it false (no `.fq-spread` ancestor → unaffected). Exposes `--fq-word-base`/`--fq-line-gap-base`/`--fq-heading-base` inline so the double-view width cap (the `html[data-safha-view="double"] .fq-spread` rule in globals.css, ADR 0013 Addenda 3–4) can shrink the reading font when two pages would overflow the viewport width. Does NOT re-group lines: `lines` already arrives grouped by the active edition's own line numbers AND composed from that edition's page assignment (ADR 0033). The previous client-side `activeLines` re-grouping mixed one edition's page composition with another's line numbers, which silently rendered words from the wrong page — never reintroduce it. Derives surah banner positions from `line_number` gaps in `lines`: missing slot numbers (1–15) are grouped into consecutive gap runs; each run is classified by looking at the first word after (start/mid gap) or last word before (end gap) — gap size + surah bismillah status determines whether to render SurahBannerLine, BismillahLine, or both. Renders SurahBannerLine / BismillahLine local helpers as direct children of .fq-quran-safha (so flex spacing counts them as real slots); passes suppressInlineHeaderForSurahId to the QuranLine immediately after each start/mid banner to prevent double-rendering of the inline combined heading block. SurahBannerLine's decorative frame is `app/surah-frame.svg` — the KFGQPC band, glyph U+E000 extracted losslessly from QUL's `quran-common.ttf`, a single `currentColor` fill driven by `--mushaf-ornament` (one colour role; the old `--surah-frame-line`/`--surah-frame-gold` tokens and their per-theme/per-band overrides are gone). Its layout slot is `1em` like any other line while its ink is ~1.81em: the SVG is absolutely centred at `width: var(--fq-surah-frame-w, 100%); height: auto`, so it spans the text column, overflows into the inter-line gaps, and contributes zero layout height. The frame's own box is `QURAN_MAX_LINE_WIDTH_RATIO` em (14.42, the measured widest line) with `maxWidth: 100%` and `mx-auto` — matching the text block, not the card's content box; `w-full` made it span the whole page on mobile/tablet where the font caps before lines fill the card (ADR 0011). `height` must stay `auto` — a hardcoded `em` height stretches the art (DECISIONS.md); shrink `--fq-surah-frame-w` if clearance is ever needed
